# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/

# public/ is generated from art_src/ by `npm run art`, but it is committed
# anyway, because it is what gets deployed.
#
# Building it in CI instead would mean installing Python, Pillow and ffmpeg
# there, and a keying bug would take the site down rather than merely looking
# wrong on somebody's machine. Committing the output costs some binary churn
# whenever art is re-rolled and means the thing deployed is exactly the thing
# that was played.

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local environment overrides
*.local
.env
.env.*

# Python bytecode from the art tooling.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Audio is held out of the repository while its licensing is confirmed.
#
# The sound effects come from Pixabay and the three music tracks have no
# identifying metadata at all -- see CREDITS.md. Bundling licensed audio in a
# game is an ordinary permitted use; publishing the .mp3 files themselves in a
# public repository is a different act, and not one to take on an assumption.
#
# The files stay on disk, so a local checkout still has sound. Delete these
# four lines to restore them once the terms are confirmed.
art_src/sfx/
art_src/music/
public/sfx/
public/music/
